"vote":"aye"},{"name":"Lidia Thorpe","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10961","person_slug":"lidia-thorpe","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Louise Pratt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10714","person_slug":"louise-pratt","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Malarndirri McCarthy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10855","person_slug":"malarndirri-mccarthy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Malcolm Roberts","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_10856","person_slug":"malcolm-roberts","vote":"no"},{"name":"Marielle Smith","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10953","person_slug":"marielle-smith","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Marise Payne","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10509","person_slug":"marise-payne","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Matt O'Sullivan","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10958","person_slug":"matt-osullivan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Matthew Canavan","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10827","person_slug":"matthew-canavan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mehreen Faruqi","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10912","person_slug":"mehreen-faruqi","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Murray Watt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10857","person_slug":"murray-watt","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nick McKim","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Patrick Dodson","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10846","person_slug":"patrick-dodson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Perin Davey","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10947","person_slug":"perin-davey","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rex Patrick","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10903","person_slug":"rex-patrick","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam McMahon","party":"Country Liberal Party","person_id":"tvfy_10948","person_slug":"sam-mcmahon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Mitochondrial Donation Law Reform (Maeve’s Law) Bill 2021 - in Committee - Inclusion in annual reports","noes":27,"question":"The majority voted in favour of keeping [item 55A](https://parlinfo.aph.gov.au/parlInfo/search/display/display.w3p;db=LEGISLATION;id=legislation%2Fbills%2Fr6697_third-reps%2F0001;query=Id%3A%22legislation%2Fbills%2Fr6697_third-reps%2F0000%22;rec=0) of schedule 1 unchanged. In parliamentary jargon, they voted that that item *stand as printed*. This was a [free vote](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/parliament-at-work/crossing-the-floor/) (also known as a conscience vote), which means our senators voted according to their own beliefs rather than strictly along party lines. ### Text of item 55A > *55A At the end of section 19* > > *Add:* > >> *(4) A report under this section must not include information about any of the following matters unless the NHMRC Licensing Committee considers that the information does not identify, and is not reasonably capable of being used to identify, any person:* > >> *(a) approvals under subsection 28P(3) (including applications for such approvals and the outcomes of those applications);* >> >> *(b) births of children as a result of pregnancies achieved using a mitochondrial donation technique under a clinical trial licence or a clinical practice licence;* >> >> *(c) adverse events notified to the NHMRC Licensing Committee under paragraph 28S(3)(a).* ### What does this bill do? According to the [bills digest](https://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd2021a/21bd065): > *Mitochondrial disease is a group of conditions that can cause serious health issues and, in severe cases, can cause death in childhood. There is no known cure for mitochondrial disease.* > > *Mitochondrial donation is an assisted reproductive technology (ART) that can assist women to avoid passing mitochondrial DNA disease to their biological child. This technology is not a cure for mitochondrial disease but is rather a way to prevent children from inheriting mitochondria that can cause mitochondrial disease.* > > *","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7604","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2022-02-10/10"}
